course: dictionary
lesson: 8604
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the words around them tell you which one is meant. The word scout is a good example. It can name a person or a club member, and it can also be an action, like looking around.
explain: «A scout ant leaves a smell trail from food to the nest» uses scout for an ant sent ahead to find food. Its job is to go first, look around and bring back news. Check it by swapping in your meaning: does «a member of a club ant» make sense? No. So scout means someone sent ahead to look around.
explain: «Scout's honour» is a phrase you may hear. It means "I promise, you can trust me." It comes from the Scouts, a club whose founder, Robert Baden-Powell, made promises central to it. The first Scout Law, in 1908, said, "A Scout's honour is to be trusted."
fact: Scout can be a noun (a person or thing) or a verb (an action word).
fact: A scout is a member of the Scouts, a club for young people who go camping, help others and earn badges.
fact: A scout is also someone sent ahead to look around and bring back news.
fact: To scout around means to look around to find something.
fact: A talent scout looks for good players or performers.
exercise: «A scout ant leaves a smell trail from food to the nest.» What is a scout ant doing? | Guarding the queen | Sleeping in the nest all day | *Going ahead to find food and show the way back | Carrying a tent on a camping trip
exercise: Mia's older brother is a Scout and goes camping every summer. What is a Scout? | A kind of tent | A bee that dances to find a new home | A talent who looks for good players | *A member of a club for young people who camp, help others and learn skills outdoors
exercise: Dad says, «Scout around for the lost keys.» What does scout around mean? | To fold up a tent | To sing loudly | To run away from home | *To look around to find something
test: «The talent scout clapped as the singer finished.» What does scout mean here? | *Someone who looks for good players or performers | A bee leaving the hive | A member of a camping club | A person who sells cookies door to door
test: What does «Scout's honour» mean? | I am a member of a camping club | I have won a badge | *I promise, you can trust me | I am looking for something lost
exam: «Scouts dance for places and the swarm picks the one with most supporters.» In a swarm of bees, what do the scouts do? | *Dance to show possible new homes, and the swarm picks one | Eat all the food in the hive | Sleep in the hive all day | Guard the queen from the rain
